WHERE THE STILL ARM'S GAP IS — the first per-class attribution taken on the
STILL binary since 2026-08-13, and it disagrees with the video-key record
about which intra kernel matters.

date:   2026-09-03
host:   mac (Apple M4 Pro, aarch64-apple-darwin, 12 cores)
commit: d56a8ef8 (main, after the three allocation-site hoists and the z1/z3
        directional-intra NEON arms)
tool:   /usr/bin/sample @1ms via tools/perf_profile/prof.sh on a steady-state
        loop of the SAME cell on each side, then selftime.py + classify.py +
        attrib.py. `<deduplicated_symbol>` is attributed to its parent frame
        (see tools/perf_profile/README.md trap 1 — leaving it unattributed
        overstated the transform gap ~2x).
cells:  gradient 512x512 qp 40, presets 2 / 6 / 10, **STILL config** — the
        default `perf_encode` avif still-picture path, no `SVTAV1_VIDEO`.
scale:  per-class ms = (class self samples / total) * the PAIRED encode ms from
        benchmarks/perf_2026-09-03-still512.tsv (n=15 interleaved paired
        rounds, ALL THREE CELLS byte-identical to C):
          512 p2   port 552.905 ms  C 174.230 ms  3.174x
          512 p6   port  33.094 ms  C  12.790 ms  2.588x
          512 p10  port   6.606 ms  C   2.601 ms  2.540x
data:   perf_still_attrib_2026-09-03.tsv (class + why tables, all three cells)
        perf_still_attrib_2026-09-03.detail.txt (per-symbol lists, both sides,
        for every class at or above 3 % of the gap)

=================== THE RANKING, BY SHARE OF THE STILL GAP ===================

  rank  512 p2                 512 p6                 512 p10
  1     DISTORTION   17.4 %    MD_DRIVER    17.0 %    MD_DRIVER    28.9 %
  2     QUANT_RDOQ   15.3 %    ALLOC        16.4 %    ALLOC        20.3 %
  3     MD_DRIVER    12.2 %    CDEF         14.2 %    LIBC_MEM     11.6 %
  4     FWD_TXFM     10.8 %    LIBC_MEM      9.9 %    FWD_TXFM      9.4 %
  5     ALLOC        10.1 %    DISTORTION    7.7 %    COEFF_CTX     9.2 %
  6     LIBC_MEM      8.4 %    FWD_TXFM      7.4 %    SYNTAX_WRITE  6.6 %
  7     INV_TXFM      6.5 %    QUANT_RDOQ    6.1 %    DISTORTION    6.2 %
  8     INTRA_PRED    6.3 %    LOOP_RESTORE  6.0 %    INTRA_PRED    6.0 %
  9     COEFF_CTX     6.2 %    INTRA_PRED    5.4 %    QUANT_RDOQ    4.3 %
  10    CDEF          4.9 %    INV_TXFM      3.6 %    RANGE_CODER   1.6 %

**ALLOC + LIBC_MEM is the only item in the top five at ALL THREE presets** —
18.5 % of the gap at p2, 26.3 % at p6, 31.9 % at p10 — and it is by far the
worst RATIO in the table: ALLOC is 387x C at p2, 52x at p6, 25x at p10, and
LIBC_MEM (memset / memmove / bzero) is 3.9-5.8x. C's ALLOC column at p2 is
0.099 ms; the port's is 38.3. Three allocation sites were hoisted earlier the
same day and this is what is LEFT.

=================== THE `why` BUCKETS ===================

  cell     SIMD_GAP   SIMD_QUAL   ALLOC    SCALAR_BOTH
  512 p2     5.3 %      33.1 %    18.1 %      43.4 %
  512 p6    11.2 %      25.4 %    25.6 %      37.8 %
  512 p10    5.1 %      20.4 %    30.7 %      43.8 %

**SIMD COVERAGE is the SMALLEST bucket on the still arm at every preset.** The
port is not mostly losing to kernels C vectorises and it does not — it is
losing to kernels BOTH sides vectorise (SIMD_QUAL, 20-33 %), to code neither
side vectorises (SCALAR_BOTH, 38-44 %), and to the allocator. Anyone planning
still-path work from the inter record's "five scalar kernels" framing will
pick the wrong queue.

=================== TWO CORRECTIONS TO THE RECORD ===================

**1. INTRA_PRED's hot symbol is PRESET-DEPENDENT, and the video-key record
named only one of the two.** At 512 p2 the port's INTRA_PRED is
`dr_predictor_edged` **763 samples** and C's counterparts are
`svt_av1_dr_prediction_z2_neon` **323**, `_z3_neon` 94, `_z1_neon` 83 — so
**z2 is C's largest directional kernel on the still arm, larger than z1 and z3
combined**, and z2 is the one this repo has NOT ported (see the z1/z3 commit's
"NOT DONE"). At 512 p6 and p10 the picture is completely different: the port's
INTRA_PRED is `predict_dc` (235), `predict_filter_intra` (161),
`predict_smooth` (126) and `dr_predictor_edged` does not appear in the top
twelve at all. **A directional-intra optimisation is a preset-2 item on the
still arm; DC / filter-intra / smooth are the p6-p10 items.**

**2. CDEF is a still-arm item at p6 and NOT at p10.** 14.2 % of the gap at p6
(6.60x) and 4.9 % at p2 (6.49x), but **0.0 %** at p10 — the still path at p10
does not run it at all. The port's `cdef_filter_block` is 828 samples at p6
against C's `svt_av1_cdef_filter_block_8xn_8_native_neon` 255 +
`_4xn_8_native_neon` 56 + the two `_bounded_neon` variants 67. Both sides are
NEON, so it is a QUALITY item — and the structural difference is visible in
the source: C works in **int16x8** lanes throughout
(`ASM_NEON/cdef_filter_block_neon.c:26`, `int16x8_t sum, res; uint16x8_t max,
min, tap, row`) where the port carries the same 8 columns as a
`[int32x4_t; 2]` pair, i.e. **twice the vector operations for the same work**.

=================== WHAT IS AND IS NOT ESTABLISHED ===================

ESTABLISHED:
  * The class and bucket shares above, for gradient 512x512 qp 40 at three
    presets on the still config, scaled by paired byte-identical encode times.
  * That ALLOC + LIBC_MEM is the largest consistent item and has the worst
    ratio.
  * That z2 is C's largest dr kernel at p2 and that dr is absent from the p6
    and p10 top twelve.

NOT ESTABLISHED, and do not quote it as if it were:
  * Any size other than 512x512, any content other than gradient, any qp but
    40. `perf_class_attrib_2026-08-13.meta` measured 1024 as well and the class
    ORDER moved with size.
  * Any A/B result. These are PROFILE SHARES. The still path has already
    taught this campaign twice that a share is not a win: `aom_hadamard_8x8`
    was 1.88 % of p2 and delivered 1.031x because its caller stayed scalar.
    Price a candidate with tools/perf_ab.sh before building it.
  * 10-bit or real content.
